          <p>
            You can stretch any of these numbers by managing loads instead of leaving everything plugged in. Running the fridge on a schedule, keeping the doors shut, unplugging the CPAP humidifier, and putting the sump pump on only during rain can easily add 30-50% to the runtime column. If you are unsure which capacity to buy, our <a href="/what-size-portable-power-station-do-i-need/">power station sizing guide</a> walks through the load list step by step.
          </p>

          <p>
            Do not trust manufacturer runtime claims that quote a single load at its minimum draw. A fridge rated at 150W running does not use 150W around the clock; it cycles. Conversely, a sump pump rated at 800W running can use far more in a day than a fridge if the pit fills quickly. The only reliable approach is daily energy, and a cheap plug-in watt meter on the fridge for a week will tell you your real number.
          </p>
